Z||000000||Cheever2||03-24-2001||04:37 PM||||Me & my 15 yr old son replaced a cracked exhaust manifold and A/C hoses on the Duke today.  Yes, folks, Cheever2 got his hands dirty!  Took a pic but you gotta be patient.  The old manifold had a gaping hole in it.  The car sure is a lot quieter now.<P>What's it cost to have the A/C recharged?<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||85Josh||03-24-2001||05:40 PM||||Congrats! I always feel like I've really aclomplished something when I fix my own cars. Besides, mechanics make more than I do! Since you opened the A/C system, you will have to get it vaccumed down, and I would look into converting to R134a, since R12 will cost around $100 for the gas alone.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4<BR>CAVALRY SCOUT!(stuck in Field Artillery)||||reg||1
Z||000002||DavidHenshaw||03-24-2001||05:53 PM||||Working on your own car can be a bi**ch but  you'll know its done right and save some money. I once had the brakes on my vw beetle done by a "reputable garage". Couple days later the pedal went to the floor with absolutely no warning. Something like that realy builds confidence.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||LarryB||03-24-2001||06:21 PM||||85Josh is right.  It'll cost you about as much to get your A/C recharged with R12 as it is to have it converted over to R134A. You can pay the man now or pay him more later. <BR>||||reg||3
